    "lawCode": "Add §75, Cor L; amd §259-j, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Correction Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S3559\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the correction law and the executive law, in relation\nto requiring persons released from prison or parole to be advised of\ntheir eligibility to vote\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nTo insure that an individual, who is a citizen of the United States,\nshall be informed of his/her right to participate in the voting\nprocess, once the individual has completed his/her sentence of\nincarceration and/or parole.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nSection 1 of the correction law is amended by adding a new section 75;\nsection 259-j of the executive law, as amended by chapter 1 of the\nlaws of 1998 is amended; section 259-j of the executive law, as\namended by chapter 396 of the laws of 1987 is amended.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nBasic constitutional principles of fairness and equal protection\nrequire an equal opportunity for citizens to be able to utilize the\nmost basic constitutional act of citizenship - their voting franchise.\nWhile one automatically regains his/her voting privileges upon\ncompletion of his/her sentence of incarceration and/or parole, the\nfact is that most are unaware of the restoration of this right.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nThis is a new bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect thirty days after it shall have become a\nlaw.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
